\f0\fs30 \cf0 # JUGGLING GAME DESIGN DOCUMENT\
\
==================================================\
CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY\
==================================================\
\
The game is built around three independent forms of progression.\
\
\'95 Strength unlocks capability.\
\'95 Accuracy unlocks consistency.\
\'95 Player skill unlocks high scores.\
\
The player should never feel that statistics alone win the game. Better stats make difficult tricks possible and more consistent, but mastering timing and juggling patterns should always provide the greatest rewards.\
\
==================================================\
CORE PLAYER STATS\
==================================================\
\
Accuracy\
- Increases the probability of successfully catching an object.\
- Determines catch consistency.\
- Continues increasing beyond 100 through the Focus mechanic.\
\
Strength\
- Determines whether heavier objects can be thrown correctly.\
- Allows higher throws with heavier objects.\
- Reduces throw inaccuracy caused by heavy objects.\
\
Endurance\
- Determines maximum stamina.\
- Allows longer practice sessions and performances.\
\
Reputation\
- Increases money earned from performances.\
- Improves after successful performances.\
- Decreases after poor performances.\
\
Speed\
- Slows gameplay from the player's perspective.\
- Maximum permanent bonus: 25%.\
\
Examples\
\
0%\
Normal gameplay.\
\
25%\
Everything moves 25% slower, giving the player 25% more reaction time.\
\
