==================================================\
OPTIONAL DIFFICULTY:\
CONTINUOUS THROW HEIGHTS\
==================================================\
\
By default, throw heights are discrete.\
\
An optional difficulty setting enables continuous throw heights.\
\
Instead of snapping to Heights 1\'965, the player may release the throw button at any point, producing fractional heights.\
\
Examples\
\
Height 3.2\
\
Height 3.6\
\
Height 4.1\
\
Height 4.8\
\
Continuous heights make throw timing significantly more difficult because object airtime and rotations vary continuously instead of matching a small set of practiced timings.\
\
This mode is intended for experienced players seeking an additional challenge.\
\
==================================================\
