comments on gameplay: the arms are way too long for some tricks. The arms can only have two positions: in and outwards, like the standard throw catch respectively. The only difference with tricks will be the throws and from where you can or throw. So: For example reverse cascade: you catch inwards position and throw outward position. the throws therefore cross eachother closely but never touch normally. Also: for all tricks and especially columns for both hands i saw a problem: a hand should only move to the other position when it is supposed because the player gives the throw or catch command. The only difference now is that not all throw commands make the hand go inwards, some patterns or tricks make it go outwards. But movement should not happen unless the player directs so. But the columns alone should have one more hand position for both hands: very inwards (almost in the middle). And the throws and catches are never made with the outwards position ; this means that columns also uses only two positions, but they are shifted one to the middle. Also: reputation: the high score should very much influence the reputation gained or lost. A very high score should grant a lot of reputation (but make sure it's impossible to unlock two venues at once), while a very low score (even with high applause) should not give that much reputation. And a low score and low applause should take away reputation. right now i feel like you can only gain reputation, although better venues should expect better juggling: make it near impossible to unlock high venues with only 3 ball juggling, you should be using 3 clubs at least, preferably 5 clubs or 3 torches. Using more objects should give your highscore and reputation a good boost if you manage it, compared to just spamming 3 balls very well, (limit easy jugglings power). Perhaps the multiplyer for consecutive perfect catches is a bit too op for 3 ball juggling, compared to how much 5 ball juggling should give you. Make the player want to move onto harder juggling patterns for their progression and MONEY; Also nerf the 60 seconds slowmo: make it 30. \
